1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,600
In 1983, Quebec had 14.2% unemployment. Third-worst of the 10 provinces.

2
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:12,700
Alberta in 2019 had 6.9%, which is fine. But the next year, 11.4%. Second-worst in the country.

3
00:00:13,700 --> 00:00:20,800
Then 2021 to 2024, four years running, the lowest unemployment in Canada was Quebec.

4
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:23,300
Nobody saw that coming. Least of all Quebec.

5
00:00:23,400 --> 00:00:30,100
Since 1976, six different provinces have had the lowest rate. And Newfoundland? Highest rate in Canada, all 50 years.

6
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:32,900
At least they're consistent, I guess.

